{"content_hash":"1f13bcfce77c0fc6c552e840f1c5a9697680b38f8b55e802a24ca41519f11d37","event_uuid":"b0c0c8ca-b7d8-4194-ad7b-7b005d18c1f4","position":{"commit_sha":"4d74bdc7a8803c313efb1d2b6e75afa4aa24fb90","position":"1784947846006231001-b0c0c8ca-b7d8-4194-ad7b-7b005d18c1f4"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"2c957aed81f4054cef49ffc9bd44f125799de472150ef23c9ee216258a52b3cf","event_uuid":"4b0b04ac-dfb5-4047-96ab-959f5b7f0f6a","position":{"commit_sha":"00fa9a659e7c464d496b39e4b2f881e6835a8a13","position":"1784950337961652001-4b0b04ac-dfb5-4047-96ab-959f5b7f0f6a"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"6b2676245b4a5dd5dc53ecba41c59d8e5be55b2e415e47a3c9627a2a30e14106","event_uuid":"532ec0d8-e781-4440-a236-09e7cf5c98ac","position":{"commit_sha":"00fa9a659e7c464d496b39e4b2f881e6835a8a13","position":"1784950338302537001-532ec0d8-e781-4440-a236-09e7cf5c98ac"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"9f11472642009862536a43714faf27b062cacee7bc5683204baa4782175d7bfc","event_uuid":"b7667453-7e03-44a7-a868-054ee7f6a0de","position":{"commit_sha":"2ac6acdaea362700cda16337ead7a2ef1702339b","position":"1784950706522916202-b7667453-7e03-44a7-a868-054ee7f6a0de"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":"claude-code_2-1-220_agent","claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":"3ca86ca0-4a66-4c30-b883-1d7f630a49fb","comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Plan review round 1 returned BLOCK on COH + G6, both pointing at the same gap: the plan dropped the epic +2 clarity bonus without showing the resulting score arithmetic.\n\nVerified empirically against the real _clarity_score rather than estimating:\n- epic fixture today (with SC block): 440 chars, score 6\n- SC block removed, bonus DROPPED: 412 chars, score 4 -- BELOW the default threshold of 5, so test_clarity_pass_implies_check_ac_pass[epic] goes RED and the fixture would need padding past 500 chars\n- SC block removed, bonus REPOINTED to Acceptance Criteria: score 6, unchanged\n\nChanged the approach from DROP to REPOINT. Repointing makes the epic bonus automatic (AC is already a universal blocking floor), so clarity-check stops discriminating for epics -- accepted deliberately, since clarity-check is slated for removal. The decisive argument against dropping is not the fixture: dropping lowers EVERY real epic in the store by 2, risking a live clarity regression across the 108 tickets this epic migrates, for the sake of a metric being deleted.\n\nPlan now carries the measured arithmetic and an AC asserting _clarity_score(fixture,'epic')==6, so the repoint is proven score-neutral instead of assumed.","timestamp":1784947416637194001}],"created_at":1784944748001942001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[],"description":"## Why\n\nTwo regexes key on the `## Success Criteria` heading and one scope extractor lists it. They are\nthe only code that READS the heading to make a decision, so until they change the heading\nremains load-bearing and the store migration cannot be verified. (One further site,\n`src/rebar/llm/evals/eval_solver.py:308`, WRITES the heading into generated eval fixtures; that\nis a producer, not a reader, and belongs to the eval-specs story — this story does not depend\non it and its AC greps deliberately do not cover it.) `_count_ac_items` already counts `- [ ]` items ONLY\nunder `## Acceptance Criteria`, so criteria written under SC never reach the P1 blocking floor\nand can never carry the `[operator-attested]` tag — collapsing the two TIGHTENS the gate.\n\n## What\n\nPoint the heading-reading code at `## Acceptance Criteria`, and update the test fixtures that\nembed `## Success Criteria` in ticket descriptions.\n\n## Scope\n\nCode:\n- `src/rebar/_engine_support/gates.py:136` — the epic branch of `_clarity_score`, currently\n  `+2` for `^##\\s+Success Criteria`.\n- `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/det_floor.py:227` — the deliberate copy of that heuristic used for\n  P1 coverage (non-blocking); the two must stay in lockstep, which the module comments require.\n- `src/rebar/llm/code_review/assemble.py:253` — `_SCOPE_HEADINGS`, which lists\n  `\"## success criteria\"` alongside `\"## acceptance criteria\"`; drop the SC entry.\n\nTest fixtures embedding the heading:\n- `tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_gate_rubric_consistency.py:4,36`\n- `tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_completion_gate.py:48`\n- `tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_close_gate_subtree.py:28`\n- `tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_close_gate_subtree_heldout.py:22`\n- `tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_close_gate_story_epic.py:29`\n- `tests/interfaces/store/test_completion_verifier.py:219,293,356,407,425,465`\n- `tests/unit/test_project_portability_criterion.py:108`\n\nOUT OF SCOPE: removing `clarity-check` entirely (separately planned). This story only stops it\nkeying on the SC heading.\n\n## Approach\n\nIn both `_clarity_score` copies the epic branch REPOINTS its `+2` from `^##\\s+Success Criteria`\nto `^##\\s+Acceptance Criteria`. Because AC is already a universal blocking floor, the bonus\nbecomes automatic and the epic branch stops discriminating. That is accepted deliberately:\nclarity-check is a dead metric already slated for removal, and the alternative is worse.\n\nThe arithmetic, measured against the real `_clarity_score` rather than estimated. The epic\nfixture in `test_gate_rubric_consistency.py` scores 6 today (heading +1, len>=200 +1,\nlen>=500 +1, bullet +1, SC +2 ... minus length, netting 6 at 440 chars). With the SC block\nremoved and the bonus DROPPED it scores 4 at 412 chars — below the default threshold of 5, so\n`test_clarity_pass_implies_check_ac_pass[epic]` goes RED and would need the fixture padded past\n500 chars to compensate. With the bonus REPOINTED it scores 6, unchanged.\n\nDropping the bonus would also lower every real epic in the store by 2, risking a live\nclarity-check regression across the 108 migrated tickets for the sake of a metric being deleted.\nRepointing avoids both the fixture fragility and that regression, so it is the chosen route.\n\n`_SCOPE_HEADINGS` loses `\"## success criteria\"`; `\"## acceptance criteria\"` already covers the\ncollapsed vocabulary.\n\nFixtures that carry BOTH headings drop the SC block; fixtures carrying SC as their only\ncriteria block have it renamed to `## Acceptance Criteria` with its bullets converted to\n`- [ ]` items so they still satisfy the P1 floor.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `test_gate_rubric_consistency.py` is the invariant that a clarity-PASS implies a check-ac\n  PASS; it must stay green with the epic fixture no longer carrying SC.\n- `pytest tests/interfaces/lifecycle tests/interfaces/store tests/unit/test_project_portability_criterion.py` green.\n- A new case pinning that an epic carrying `## Acceptance Criteria` plus `## Context` (the two\n  remaining epic signals) passes BOTH `clarity-check` and `check-ac`. The fixture deliberately\n  keeps `## Context` so the case tests the AC repoint rather than the degenerate\n  zero-heading-signal path.\n- An assertion of the score itself (`_clarity_score(fixture, \"epic\") == 6`), so a future change\n  to the weights fails loudly here instead of silently drifting the epic fixture under the\n  threshold.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `grep -rn \"Success Criteria\" src/rebar/_engine_support/gates.py src/rebar/llm/plan_review/det_floor.py src/rebar/llm/code_review/assemble.py` returns no matches.\n- [ ] The two `_clarity_score` copies remain textually in lockstep (verified by diffing the two\n      epic branches), preserving the invariant their comments assert.\n- [ ] No test file under `tests/interfaces/lifecycle/`, `tests/interfaces/store/` or\n      `tests/unit/test_project_portability_criterion.py` contains `## Success Criteria`.\n- [ ] A new test asserts an epic whose description carries `## Acceptance Criteria` and\n      `## Context` passes both `clarity-check` and `check-ac` (exit 0 each), and that\n      `_clarity_score(fixture, \"epic\")` equals 6 — the same score the fixture earns today, so\n      the repoint is proven score-neutral rather than assumed.\n- [ ] The epic fixture in `test_gate_rubric_consistency.py` needs NO length padding to stay\n      green, confirming the repoint (not a drop) was implemented.\n- [ ] `make lint`, `make typecheck` and the full pytest suite pass.","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_engine_support/gates.py","reason":"Epic branch of _clarity_score drops the SC heading bonus"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/plan_review/det_floor.py","reason":"Lockstep copy of the clarity heuristic"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/code_review/assemble.py","reason":"Drop SC from _SCOPE_HEADINGS"},{"path":"tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_gate_rubric_consistency.py","reason":"Epic fixture drops SC"},{"path":"tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_completion_gate.py","reason":"Fixture heading"},{"path":"tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_close_gate_subtree.py","reason":"Fixture heading"},{"path":"tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_close_gate_subtree_heldout.py","reason":"Fixture heading"},{"path":"tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_close_gate_story_epic.py","reason":"Fixture heading"},{"path":"tests/interfaces/store/test_completion_verifier.py","reason":"Six fixture sites"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_project_portability_criterion.py","reason":"Fixture heading"}],"keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","managed_refs":[["parent","1386-5e7c-391d-4a74"]],"parent_id":"1386-5e7c-391d-4a74","parent_status_uuid":"4b0b04ac-dfb5-4047-96ab-959f5b7f0f6a","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["vocabulary","plan-review"],"ticket_id":"35bc-aef6-efd5-4df5","ticket_type":"story","title":"Point heading-detection code and its test corpus at Acceptance Criteria","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["9187ded9-4072-4fb8-8385-068567c2f7b7","8dc16899-35f5-41c9-b90f-9e6bff227fac","6023eddf-62df-4c98-a23c-30df32b07884","cff9fdc2-9a00-4581-ba14-57a2b4442bd4","1e650deb-db5d-4818-b55b-f283694a1666","891f17b4-6eb4-4c07-ae8c-f3aa2216052a","b0c0c8ca-b7d8-4194-ad7b-7b005d18c1f4","4b0b04ac-dfb5-4047-96ab-959f5b7f0f6a","532ec0d8-e781-4440-a236-09e7cf5c98ac","b7667453-7e03-44a7-a868-054ee7f6a0de"]},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1784950706522916203,"uuid":"64059298-2118-4fb5-ba99-ee1b1809c7ed"}